{"name":"Light Bright Spark","hex":"#94d0e9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"light","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye (about 400–750 nanometers): visible light.","Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye or in nearby ranges (infrared or ultraviolet radiation)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To start (a fire).","To set fire to; to set burning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/light"},{"term":"bright","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Emitting much light; visually dazzling; luminous, lucent, radiant.","Of light: brilliant, intense."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Brightness, glow.\n\n Glory, splendour.","Brightness, glow."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bright"},{"term":"spark","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small particle of glowing matter, either molten or on fire, resulting from an electrical surge or excessive heat created by friction.","A short or small burst of electrical discharge."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To trigger, kindle into activity (an argument, etc).","To light; to kindle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spark"}],"entries":[{"title":"Spark (fire)","blocks":[{"text":"A spark is an incandescent particle. Sparks may be produced by pyrotechnics, by metalworking or as a by-product of fires, especially when burning wood."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Sparks_from_a_Grinder.jpg/330px-Sparks_from_a_Grinder.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spark_(fire)","wikidata":"Q911679"},{"title":"Light","blocks":[{"text":"Light, visible light, or visible radiation is electromagnetic radiation that can be perceived by the human eye. Visible light spans the visible spectrum and is usually defined as having wavelengths